Paragraph (1) what is meant by "physical violence" is any act that results in pain, injury, wounds or disability to a person's body, miscarriage, fainting and or causes death. What is meant by "psychological violence" is an act that results in fear, loss of self-confidence, loss of ability to act, feelings of helplessness and or severe psychological suffering to a person. What is meant by "sexual violence" is any act in the form of sexual harassment, forced sexual relations, forced sexual relations in an unnatural or unwanted manner, forced sexual relations with others for commercial purposes and or certain purposes. What is meant by "exploitation" includes: acts that exploit a child economically or sexually with the intention of benefiting oneself or others;
